  "description": "Examines Olduvai fossils, stone tools and modified bones alongside Laetoli footprints, showing how stratigraphy, isotopic dating, taphonomy and track mechanics constrain inferences about early hominins. Distinguishes fossil classification from attribution of tool-making and examines the reassessment of Site A and the additional Site S trackways.",
